  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** WhiteFiber is riding a powerful wave of AI infrastructure demand, with momentum concentrated in cloud services and colocation. The NC-1 data center project is the central growth catalyst, on track to begin serving a large, long-term contract with Nscale as power delivery milestones are met. This underpins a substantial contracted backlog, though it also creates a meaningful customer concentration risk. While the operating environment remains favorable for AI compute providers, the company must eventually demonstrate it can fill expanded capacity beyond its anchor tenant, and broader competitive and macro uncertainties linger over the sector.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is executing a build-and-contract strategy, advancing NC-1 through construction and commissioning while securing the power and anchor tenant needed for scale. The CEO emphasizes investment in the AI platform even as the company delivered positive adjusted EBITDA. Capital allocation has focused on de-risking the balance sheet, with a convertible notes offering and new credit facilities shoring up liquidity to fund the infrastructure build-out. Market reaction to earnings was mixed—strong top-line progress was offset by an earnings miss—but management’s ability to lock in large contractual commitments is drawing analyst support and raised price targets.",
